for each iteration."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The batched sequence listens to the subject without owning it: when the batched sequence","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ends or is cancelled, its wait ends at once and the subject stays pending for its other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"awaiters. A subject sent an error ends the batched sequence with that error, except","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (as when another awaiter cancels the subject): then the signal stops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"firing and the batches go on. A subject sent a value before iteration begins fires when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"signal’s task starts, which may come after elements have arrived, so the first batch may be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"short. Each batched sequence iterated with this strategy listens anew, so a subject","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already sent a value fires again when a later batched sequence’s signal task starts.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Example","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Example"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let shutdown = SingleValueSubject<Void>()","for try await messages in inbox.batch(strategy: .either(.count(50), .signal(shutdown))) {","    store(messages)","}","\/\/ Elsewhere: flush whatever is pending before shutting down.","try shutdown.send()"],"type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/signalbatchstrategy\/signal(_:)-7c9kk"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Flushes once, when the given subject is sent a value."}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\